counterfactuals.output:
A daylighting film comprising:

a first base layer; and

a plurality of elongated prism structures disposed on the first base layer, adjacent ones of the plurality of elongated prism structures being separated from one another by respective gaps;

wherein each elongated prism structure has a length extending along a longitudinal direction and a cross-sectional profile, taken in a plane transverse to the longitudinal direction, that is quadrilateral and includes four interior angles, each of the four interior angles being less than 180 degrees;

wherein each elongated prism structure includes a base side coupled to or formed integrally with the first base layer; and

wherein each elongated prism structure includes an asymmetric peak geometry such that, in the cross-sectional profile, a peak of the elongated prism structure is laterally offset relative to a midpoint of the base side or such that opposing side surfaces extending toward the peak have different slopes, lengths, curvatures, or angular orientations.

A daylighting film comprising:

a first base (2) having a first principal surface and a second principal surface opposite to the first principal surface; and

a plurality of daylighting portions (3) provided on the first principal surface of the first base (2),

wherein each of the daylighting portions (3) is formed as a polygonal prism extending in a predetermined longitudinal direction, the polygonal prism having a cross-sectional shape, in a plane perpendicular to the longitudinal direction, defined by a plurality of sides and a plurality of vertices;

wherein the plurality of daylighting portions (3) are arranged on the first base (2) at intervals so that gaps (9) are provided between adjacent daylighting portions (3);

wherein, in the cross-sectional shape of each daylighting portion (3), a side located adjacent to the first base (2) is defined as a first side, and two end points of the first side are defined as first and second vertices;

wherein a vertex of the polygonal cross-section located farthest from the first side in a direction normal to the first base (2) is defined as a third vertex;

wherein a first perpendicular line is a line passing through the first vertex and extending perpendicular to the first side, and a second perpendicular line is a line passing through the second vertex and extending perpendicular to the first side;

wherein the third vertex is positioned between the first perpendicular line and the second perpendicular line, as viewed in the cross-section perpendicular to the longitudinal direction; and

wherein the cross-sectional shape of each daylighting portion (3) is asymmetrical with respect to a perpendicular bisector of the first side, such that a light incident surface and a light reflecting or light redirecting surface of the daylighting portion (3) have different inclinations relative to the first side, thereby causing incident daylight to be refracted, reflected, or redirected in a predetermined direction through the daylighting film.
